# Scratch-file patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern with no
# slash matches at ANY depth: a bare junit.xml in a product .gitignore silently
# excluded a required committed fixture in P060 of this mission, and a cold
# clone then failed with 17 failures and 9 errors while every local check
# passed. validation/validate_tree_hygiene.py checks both directions, with the
# .gitignore semantics re-implemented rather than delegated to a git command,
# because the build agent for this product is forbidden from running git.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.pytest_cache/
/.hypothesis/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
/.config/
# This product ships no serialised model and no learned component at all: the
# registry records ai_enabled: false, and the reason is in SPEC.md section 5.
# These patterns exist so a future change cannot add one silently.
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.joblib
# The audit's machine-readable evidence is NOT ignored. It is this product's
# record of what the audit found over this repository, and
# validate_repository_findings.py pins its contents as literals, so it must
# reach a cold clone. It is listed as a negation so that a future broad pattern
# cannot swallow it silently.
!/validation/repository_findings.json
# Every validation script's raw output is evidence and must ship.
!/validation/*_output.txt
# The campaign in data/ is a data generator, not a validation script. Its
# program and the transcript of the run that produced the committed evidence
# are both evidence and must reach a cold clone.
!/data/repository_audit.py
!/data/repository_audit_output.txt
